  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Plotting the data of the given value we have,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/13e53736-24de-49d2-9fd2-e337b1bda8a4-image.png\" style=\"width: 189px; height: 120px;\" /></p><p>Now let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;be foot of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8869;</mo></math>coordinates, so given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now direction ratio of line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"&#62;\" open=\"&#60;\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced close=\"&#62;\" open=\"&#60;\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced close=\"&#62;\" open=\"&#60;\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Now comparing with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So equation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;which is passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>So point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;but given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;lies on the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, so on satisfying the point we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now finding the distance between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>26</mn></msqrt></math></p></blockquote>",
